      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 4th arrondissement houses the historic Jewish Quarter, where kosher butchers, Judaica shops, and synagogues preserve centuries of heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://metropolitanpropertiesparis.com/fourth-arrondissement-paris/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Île Saint-Louis, known for its charming streets and pastel‑colored houses, is entirely within the 4th arrondissement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4th_arrondissement_of_Paris",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Renaissance‑era Paris City Hall, rebuilt between 1874 and 1882, stands in the 4th arrondissement and is a landmark of the area’s architectural history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4th_arrondissement_of_Paris",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 4th arrondissement’s medieval street patterns and Gothic monuments give the neighborhood a distinctly historic feel that feels alive to visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4th_arrondissement_of_Paris",
